  "description": "WildSAT is a remote sensing foundation model that learns satellite image representations by leveraging millions of geo-tagged wildlife observations, environmental covariates, and text descriptions of species habitats. It uses a contrastive learning framework to align satellite images, text, and location embeddings, enabling improved downstream performance and zero-shot retrieval.",
